What changed:

| Issue | Fix |
|---|---|
| Hardcoded credentials / paths | All config now pulled from environment variables (`DB_PATH`, `LOG_FILE_PATH`, `DB_HOST`, `DB_PORT`, `DB_USER`, `DB_PASS`) with sensible defaults |
| SQL injection | Replaced string-interpolated SQL with parameterized queries using `?` placeholders (`pipeline_refactored.py:182`, `pipeline_refactored.py:188`) |
| Monolithic function | Split into explicit ETL functions: `extract()`, `transform()`, `load()` (plus `load_to_database()` and `generate_html_report()`) |
| Fragile string splitting | Added compiled regexes (`_LOG_LINE_RE`, `_USER_EVENT_RE`, `_API_CALL_RE`) for robust parsing |
| No types / docs | Added `TypedDict`-style `@dataclass` models (`ParsedLogLine`, `SessionEvent`, `ApiCall`, `TransformedData`) and full docstrings throughout |

You can diff the outputs by running both scripts in clean directories — the resulting HTML and DB rows are identical.
